  "id": "pr-298",
  "instruction": "Update glom.core so every PathAccessError can be converted to a readable string, including when its access path originated from a scope or is a T-expression/callable that cannot be represented as a plain dot-delimited path. While formatting the error, attempt the normal plain-path rendering when applicable, but safely fall back to a representation of the original access expression/path if path conversion or lookup fails; formatting must never re-raise the conversion exception or otherwise crash. Preserve the existing message and rendering for ordinary plain paths. Ensure scope-originated PathAccessError instances are printable, and that str(error) always returns a string rather than raising. Add or update coverage for the non-path fallback and scope-originated printable error behavior; unrelated existing failures do not need to be addressed.",
